tions in the statement below that describe an **unstable** equilibrium point.Some solutions starting\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\neventually\n{{field-3}}\nthe equilibrium." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the definitions of stability:\n\n- An equilibrium point ${x}^{∗}$ is called *stable* if for any neighborhood $O$ of ${x}^{∗},$ there exists a neighborhood ${O}_{1}⊆O$ such that every orbit that begins inside ${O}_{1}$ at some point in time $t={t}_{0}$ remains inside $O$ for all $t>{t}_{0}.$\n\nIn plain words, this means that solutions that start sufficiently close to the equilibrium remain close, but may not converge to the equilibrium.\n\n- An equilibrium point ${x}^{∗}$ is called *asymptotically stable* if it is stable and there exists a neighborhood $O$ of ${x}^{∗}$ such that every orbit that begins inside $O$ approaches ${x}^{∗}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nIn plain words, this means that solutions that start sufficiently close to the equilibrium remain close and converge to the equilibrium as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n- An equilibrium point ${x}^{∗}$ is called *unstable* if it is not stable.\n\nIn plain words, this means that solutions eventually move away from the equilibrium for some initial conditions arbitrarily close to it.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\nSome solutions starting $\\text{arbitrarily close to}$ $\\text{the equilibrium}$ eventually $\\text{move away from}$ the equilibrium."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396883 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "787c0213-46a5-50ef-8592-60c9965170f0" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing a Falling Body Model With Linear Drag"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065920c3-3946-51c8-a133-68edfc9cd6b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{kg/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396885} {:answer/id #uuid "0d22f601-64a5-507d-b229-bb37752252fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{s/m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396886} {:answer/id #uuid "b8a98c26-74a6-5cc7-bd61-0b52f4f896ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\text{kg/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396887} {:answer/id #uuid "2f4de62e-7406-574c-9890-752f72463e75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396888} {:answer/id #uuid "c4ca2c26-8790-5084-bf59-05857f6422a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "065920c3-3946-51c8-a133-68edfc9cd6b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{kg/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396885} :answer-field/id #uuid "af554e6b-2c53-5353-a213-81ba8542e5c0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35d84a91-a48c-5442-ba12-46ed4951dd83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396891} {:answer/id #uuid "de3ab691-ae02-5e93-b61d-565249937a19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396892} {:answer/id #uuid "fff9606c-86b6-58cf-8faa-74c6c2b26b06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396893} {:answer/id #uuid "4e61cb73-419a-52d3-a9f7-333b057968e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396894} {:answer/id #uuid "876d4332-2399-5b6f-8c02-a57015c7a565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35d84a91-a48c-5442-ba12-46ed4951dd83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396891} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f9cc258-a83b-5feb-ad2a-e5812b2c952b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396890} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8cb5870-7d7e-5f93-9c6a-f0f887130056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dv}{dt}+\\frac{1}{3}v=g" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396897} {:answer/id #uuid "35beaf44-402a-5d52-b1c7-4ebecfa4c887" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dv}{dt}+\\frac{1}{16}v=g" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396898} {:answer/id #uuid "51560195-657c-5865-98a3-9f67f3c4003a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dv}{dt}+v=g" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396899} {:answer/id #uuid "b6e0ec5c-2874-5410-b0de-b4a739e627e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dv}{dt}+\\frac{1}{4}v=g" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8cb5870-7d7e-5f93-9c6a-f0f887130056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{dv}{dt}+\\frac{1}{3}v=g" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396897} :answer-field/id #uuid "af529f9f-fe46-5674-b9c2-cb11914422f2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396896}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0989f91d-6c3f-5d3f-bed3-87412bdd7915" :question/math-academy-id "q-335748" :question/problem "A sensor pod of mass $16\\,\\text{kg}$ falls vertically downward. Let $v(t)$ be the pod's velocity, in meters per second, $t\\ge 0$ seconds after the descent began, with downward taken as the positive direction.\nThe air resistance on the pod is proportional to its velocity with a constant of proportionality $k>0$ and acts in the direction opposite to motion.\nAt a particular moment during the fall, the pod’s velocity is $6\\,\\text{m/s}$ and instantaneous acceleration is $7.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nFind the constant of proportionality $k,$ and the differential equation that best models the velocity. Assume the acceleration due to gravity is $g=9.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ and the only forces acting on the pod are weight due to gravity and drag.\n\n$\\,$ The constant of proportionality is $k=$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ The differential equation that best models the velocity is\n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall Newton's second law, which states that the resultant force $F$ acting on a body equals the product of its mass $m$ and acceleration $a:$\n\n$$\nF=ma\n$$\n\nIn our case, there are two forces acting on the body:\n\n- The force due to gravity, given by the weight $w$ of the body, which equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =mg \\\\  & =16g.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The force due to drag (air resistance) $D,$ which is proportional to the velocity of the body (and negative since it acts in the negative direction):\n\n$$\nD=-kv,\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality. Note that, since the drag, in $N=\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ is the product of the constant $k$ and velocity, in $\\text{m/s},$ the units of $k$ are\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{N}}{\\text{m/s}}=\\frac{\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m/s}}^{2}}{\\text{m/s}}=\\text{kg/s}.\n$$\n\nSumming the forces, the resultant force acting on the body is\n\n$$\nF=w+D=16g-kv.\n$$\n\nAlso, recall that acceleration is the derivative of velocity: $a=\\frac{dv}{dt}.$\nSubstituting this into Newton's second law, along with our expression for the resultant force on the body, we have\n\n$$\n16g-kv=16\\,\\frac{dv}{dt}.\n$$\n\nWriting in standard form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16\\,\\frac{dv}{dt}+kv & =16g \\\\ \\frac{dv}{dt}+\\frac{k}{16}v & =g.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we're given that, at a particular moment, the body's velocity is $6\\,\\text{m/s}$ and instantaneous acceleration is $7.8\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\nSo, substituting $v=6,g=9.8,$ and $\\frac{dv}{dt}=7.8$ into our model, we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7.8+\\frac{k}{16}\\cdot 6 & =9.8 \\\\ 7.8+\\frac{3k}{8} & =9.8 \\\\ \\frac{3k}{8} & =2 \\\\ k & =\\frac{16}{3}\\,\\text{kg/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the differential equation that models the velocity is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dv}{dt}+\\frac{1}{3}v=g.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396901 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5852157-70f8-5e93-89b0-59d8b774ff3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating the given system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396903} {:answer/id #uuid "990ecc42-c4e6-5578-a0da-d91b13097a44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding the vectors ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396904} {:answer/id #uuid "7722083e-e7dc-572c-9e33-46131eb0f8b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying $Φ(t)$ with it's inverse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396905} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d2992c-33d6-5911-8f6b-9bda3e200baa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7d2992c-33d6-5911-8f6b-9bda3e200baa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396906} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3682025-d096-56bd-bf59-0048dee77ced" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396902} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea29c33a-1099-547c-826a-fd0e927691bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Φ}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396908} {:answer/id #uuid "eda2dd9e-6754-5d8c-bfd6-9ae76f866cf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396909} {:answer/id #uuid "5c373e55-b761-5339-b7ae-18f49f46ac45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396910} {:answer/id #uuid "f31c325d-17cf-5219-a1cb-6658f11fd045" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Φ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f31c325d-17cf-5219-a1cb-6658f11fd045" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Φ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396911} :answer-field/id #uuid "eedfdc9d-7a1b-5144-98ef-079b39f1a6cd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396907} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42514761-6af9-5f0a-acd2-e9be42e06afe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of invertible matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396913} {:answer/id #uuid "7caef4bf-95b8-571b-aaa3-5210003d59f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "properties of diagonalizable matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396914} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7d92b1-be8e-5617-880a-12beb90f314b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396915} {:answer/id #uuid "47b36cde-80ca-5b95-9fb8-d497515c1778" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca7d92b1-be8e-5617-880a-12beb90f314b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of a fundamental matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396915} :answer-field/id #uuid "25b2d3de-e14d-5e49-b765-fcc7eb25aafa" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396912} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "452a40cb-853e-5f67-a98a-fbeeccb65acb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first row" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396918} {:answer/id #uuid "a4c30172-18f7-52e1-95bc-79d14f8a4bcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "diagonals" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396919} {:answer/id #uuid "c2045390-0f53-5f3d-8afa-92c13462bafa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "columns" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396920} {:answer/id #uuid "c0a29805-59cc-5557-a9b9-6313452c9c94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "rows" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2045390-0f53-5f3d-8afa-92c13462bafa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "columns" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396920} :answer-field/id #uuid "c98b9a18-7c6a-59cb-8ce5-cb6ffe8a471b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "accc1e17-f130-5583-b331-4d6a4ed72254" :question/math-academy-id "q-336106" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that every solution $x(t)$ can be written in the form $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c=[{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}]^{T}$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of solutions\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)$ can be written as $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)\\,c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ introduces the notation for the {{field-1}} of {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first interpret line $\\text{L1}.$ Line $\\text{L1}$ introduces the notation for the $\\text{columns}$ of $Φ,$ namely the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ These functions are the fundamental solutions of the system.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Once ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis, every solution $x(t)$ of the system can be expressed uniquely as a linear combination\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{the definition of a basis}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396922 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0aea7503-74d6-5ba4-9411-ee53e59512d0" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Properties of a Fundamental Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c886e4d-ec71-526e-9fca-44411eb71087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396924} {:answer/id #uuid "3ee05532-dfb9-529e-b73c-929366f56b5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396925} {:answer/id #uuid "1c690c80-9317-5e41-aaae-07f5c0248385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396926} {:answer/id #uuid "da083ae6-571f-54bb-bc13-27bab5c4d1b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c690c80-9317-5e41-aaae-07f5c0248385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396926} :answer-field/id #uuid "319112f1-c5cd-5b59-bc98-0fbaa63699a8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396923} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f41205b8-acc0-5664-955b-74b059485116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396929} {:answer/id #uuid "82374921-7bf9-535e-9301-cd8fcd3d1de9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the properties of determinants" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396930} {:answer/id #uuid "6e8e658e-f066-597f-abf6-933f8b8713c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property of equality" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396931} {:answer/id #uuid "1a09ff54-d141-5e15-a5d8-b2bb7e05d498" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e8e658e-f066-597f-abf6-933f8b8713c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the transitive property of equality" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396931} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c455c64-6a5a-53e9-8592-0cd96bbb254d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396928} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3dfad07-3750-584e-9f6f-d30755695967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating the given system" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396934} {:answer/id #uuid "995b3536-4529-5769-9f9a-f34c8177e004" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying $Φ(t)$ with it's inverse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396935} {:answer/id #uuid "dd384e88-52b2-55f6-8382-7ee54663a081" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the definition of a basis" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396936} {:answer/id #uuid "83c3e129-5f38-5e53-b0a2-61bbd06b2d41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83c3e129-5f38-5e53-b0a2-61bbd06b2d41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "definition of matrix multiplication" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396937} :answer-field/id #uuid "f108e315-8611-579e-a41e-01f211239093" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396933} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "638ac533-2df7-530f-9f02-d6db96ca8dd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396939} {:answer/id #uuid "fe02d4db-11ef-5015-aea5-bf6b6e4b9f87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396940} {:answer/id #uuid "1a1b6e19-58ed-5e2e-97f8-48746da9e753" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "638ac533-2df7-530f-9f02-d6db96ca8dd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396939} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe7c7b3b-bbe4-57bb-8ae1-e9580b65ffd9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9fcd6208-dde9-5e8a-b2c1-ff9f0dade0db" :question/math-academy-id "q-336107" :question/problem "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that every solution $x(t)$ can be written in the form $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c=[{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}]^{T}$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of solutions\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)$ can be written as $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)\\,c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from {{field-1}} by the definition of a fundamental matrix.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines {{field-3}} by {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the definition of a fundamental matrix.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are the columns of $Φ(t),$ we can write\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen by the definition of matrix multiplication,\n\n$$\nΦ(t)\\,c=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of matrix multiplication}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ In $\\text{L3}$ we have $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t),$ and in $\\text{L4}$ we have $Φ(t)c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).$ Since both expressions are equal to the same quantity, the transitive property of equality gives $x(t)=Φ(t)c.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L3 and L4}$ by the $\\text{the transitive property of equality}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396942 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c" :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution: Homogeneous Systems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "614d6ab5-5628-5fbe-818a-c13fdda2c28e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396944} {:answer/id #uuid "ce094f55-879b-5b96-bedb-c8a97168bac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396945} {:answer/id #uuid "cccff4fe-20c3-5cb7-9681-92cc25121511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396946} {:answer/id #uuid "ab84e7ed-d6a8-520d-8b8d-917218916f48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce094f55-879b-5b96-bedb-c8a97168bac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396945} :answer-field/id #uuid "62e5d724-e4aa-50ec-8d98-2ca352e011f4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396943} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3461c8f3-6347-5cda-a1c7-cd2ab24c6c21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396949} {:answer/id #uuid "41161c5d-5b28-5637-adb6-191d50f983ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396950} {:answer/id #uuid "411ea3ea-3c55-50ae-abd5-5130b8a1d446" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396951} {:answer/id #uuid "a18ae187-4ca1-50ee-ba3f-d6af9219c439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating the equation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41161c5d-5b28-5637-adb6-191d50f983ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396950} :answer-field/id #uuid "d10c4b52-29cf-597a-97d0-5df761b842ca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396948} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5363f0a4-bc32-5773-a19c-82bd214aee7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396954} {:answer/id #uuid "83b75a12-331a-52aa-8a26-b868726772a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying the chain rule" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396955} {:answer/id #uuid "9f3f9f52-0d94-5534-85e6-03b3ff052905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "using diagonalization of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396956} {:answer/id #uuid "c4e0fc6c-fed0-5c5b-bab5-4daeb2418d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating the equation" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5363f0a4-bc32-5773-a19c-82bd214aee7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating both sides at $t=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396954} :answer-field/id #uuid "b441f599-459e-58bd-b0d0-12769ed6a804" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b476f440-04ac-55c0-bbfe-8012f8f71f27" :question/math-academy-id "q-336477" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$  \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by  {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by substitution from lines {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from $\\text{L2},$ we have the identity\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c.\n$$\n\nEvaluating this identity at $t=0$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly line $\\text{L3}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{evaluating both sides at }t=0.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$, $\\text{L4},$ and $\\text{L5}.$ From $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c,\n$$\n\nand from $\\text{L4}$ we know ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$ into $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c$ gives\n\n$$\nx(0)={I}_{n}c=c,\n$$\n\nwhich is exactly line $\\text{L5}.$ Thus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$ by $\\text{substituting }{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}\\text{ into }x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)c.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$, $\\text{L2},$ $\\text{L5},$ and $\\text{L6}.$ From $\\text{L1}$ we have ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At},$ and from $\\text{L5}$ we know $c=x(0).$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ from $\\text{L1}$ and $c=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$ into $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ (line $\\text{L2}$), we obtain\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ and substitution from $\\text{L1}\\text{ and }\\text{L5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c20cd9a-5734-5129-93db-55f6dc985b3a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing the Formulas for Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b41ef18b-4fd8-5f85-9118-8892db11b4c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "line $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396959} {:answer/id #uuid "d93b8a1a-4307-506a-b249-296d73fda268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396960} {:answer/id #uuid "69db23bb-9f00-5ed5-a314-a4398d8cb228" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "solution of the system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396961} {:answer/id #uuid "3a963511-ca8a-5ebc-85ff-04e4527811af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first shifting theorem" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d93b8a1a-4307-506a-b249-296d73fda268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396960} :answer-field/id #uuid "15760b45-942f-5371-a4af-6567ed71b662" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396958} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73fc77df-9183-5392-9f5f-84c6b7225cb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a fundamental" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396964} {:answer/id #uuid "33ab2692-3bf2-5c51-81e7-2d7540647496" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a square" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396965} {:answer/id #uuid "7b292260-1158-5bf9-8ff9-6e83083ce40c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is an invertible" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396966} {:answer/id #uuid "0e5ac2ca-d399-5fa8-b244-bbd050e7ea77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ is the identity" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73fc77df-9183-5392-9f5f-84c6b7225cb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Φ$ is a fundamental" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396964} :answer-field/id #uuid "369c338a-25f1-56f5-856e-c6afcea5d80e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396963} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8aa0013e-2425-55c4-9d94-e57a745924bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396969} {:answer/id #uuid "6e4fa214-db95-5f01-97b9-814c953c2a28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396970} {:answer/id #uuid "722383ab-f057-5be9-88d9-1807d49eabbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396971} {:answer/id #uuid "96b39a06-7a60-5b50-821a-8591067e9eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96b39a06-7a60-5b50-821a-8591067e9eef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396972} :answer-field/id #uuid "65afa9b7-d90a-53f3-b255-4185b375d4c8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396968} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dd43670-1646-534f-9b82-0ec4c2ab4066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396974} {:answer/id #uuid "fabeb164-e1c7-5722-8dd4-7476a0c9cdb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396975} {:answer/id #uuid "0314521e-1ee3-553c-a49a-28490b5dc131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396976} {:answer/id #uuid "b70f4cdd-82f4-5102-b82d-3bb67d075165" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0314521e-1ee3-553c-a49a-28490b5dc131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396976} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd7b65f1-ae60-595f-b010-b4d039e76cf4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f3e98464-6e85-513e-a930-d0947c1c72b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-336711" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-1}} both sides of  the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that {{field-4}} matrix." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ To get $\\text{L2},$ we are $\\text{differentiating}$ with respect to $t$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =(Φu(t))^{′} \\\\ {x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L2},$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Let's substitute ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$ from $\\text{L1}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ into the initial system of ODEs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =Ax(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t) & =AΦu(t)+f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into $\\text{initial system of ODEs}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are linearly independent. So, $Φ$ is invertible. Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{pre-multiplying by }{Φ}^{-1}$ both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\cdot Φ{u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ ({Φ}^{-1}Φ)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are solutions to the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ i.e., by substituting any column $c(t)$ of $Φ$ into the homogeneous system, we get\n\n$$\n{c}^{′}(t)=Ac(t),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}^{′}(t)$ is the corresponding column of derivatives in $Φ.$ As a result, this means that ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that $Φ\\text{ is a fundamental}$ matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c20cd9a-5734-5129-93db-55f6dc985b3a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing the Formulas for Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cad9d195-9c91-5200-8667-b1a991261f11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396980} {:answer/id #uuid "68556745-4530-55da-ac24-38d37038b33a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396981} {:answer/id #uuid "04a2a1fa-05d3-5caf-802d-b281aaf8f532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396982} {:answer/id #uuid "cfdd0c3c-942e-5b0b-87e1-55d9e7172922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68556745-4530-55da-ac24-38d37038b33a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396981} :answer-field/id #uuid "78540bb9-06e5-582a-8e49-d50e3c4417c5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396979} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c964dd4-f3bf-52d0-8a48-08a0d9dce4ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396985} {:answer/id #uuid "07b54212-e266-5b2a-b130-c80f4063c032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396986} {:answer/id #uuid "09fc9119-29d9-586b-a809-3c6a0d6f08c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396987} {:answer/id #uuid "8576620c-99de-5e46-af59-dd2a04447008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07b54212-e266-5b2a-b130-c80f4063c032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396986} :answer-field/id #uuid "104e3546-d98c-5689-8946-72bdce35a1e0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396984} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a7f2e0a-aa8d-5e35-a60a-5265207529e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396990} {:answer/id #uuid "0daf7117-99ea-5ba6-a74b-fb851988a298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396991} {:answer/id #uuid "bfaeedd1-1cf0-5597-adbf-886c9865888b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396992} {:answer/id #uuid "c8a52c32-4263-5deb-99be-91d902304f59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396993}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a7f2e0a-aa8d-5e35-a60a-5265207529e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{L1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396990} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa75475c-51ab-516a-9842-72a619727da2" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396989} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "366556bb-2a55-5f0c-b8af-72953341d876" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396995} {:answer/id #uuid "8f129d78-0543-5e5d-b104-b1db1ae97c16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396996} {:answer/id #uuid "0d939037-0da2-5057-ad9c-0d41dcd03630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396997} {:answer/id #uuid "0138b58b-3ab3-5e16-b235-2137b6f9b6a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d939037-0da2-5057-ad9c-0d41dcd03630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396997} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f3b7f62-72d0-5d1f-849a-b5f2335de2d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "68ae00aa-e57d-5620-9c00-ead6febaac73" :question/math-academy-id "q-336716" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-1}} both sides of  the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-2}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting {{field-3}} into {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ To get $\\text{L2},$ we are $\\text{differentiating}$ with respect to $t$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =(Φu(t))^{′} \\\\ {x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L7},$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Substituting\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φu(t) \\\\  & =Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L7}$ into $\\text{L1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c" :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution: Homogeneous Systems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04e051ba-0925-5595-906b-3d9455a124a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating $x(t)={e}^{At}c$ at $t={t}_{0}$ and solving for $c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397001} {:answer/id #uuid "d66a48e9-3064-577b-a301-18a4163c2103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "left-multiplying $x(t)={e}^{At}c$ by ${e}^{-At}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397002} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7095a3-cb4a-563f-95e4-6050e0d49c1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})$ into $x(t)={e}^{At}c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d7095a3-cb4a-563f-95e4-6050e0d49c1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "substituting $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})$ into $x(t)={e}^{At}c$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397003} :answer-field/id #uuid "4034d58e-9aa0-5353-8a0b-15f70b5c05f7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397000} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3edeee75-ae1a-5118-aee9-95210f022f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating $x(t)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397005} {:answer/id #uuid "c912b961-6fae-5a81-9c28-18263ad2be59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "using the identity $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397006} {:answer/id #uuid "f7ef72cb-85ae-57ec-9183-3da0d974a189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides on the left by $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7ef72cb-85ae-57ec-9183-3da0d974a189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplying both sides on the left by $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397007} :answer-field/id #uuid "93f0bbfe-0cb3-5b50-90de-16b15a59b4bb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397004} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "875b1271-178f-5292-86cb-7fb9f34b060b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the identity ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{XY}$ for matrices" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397009} {:answer/id #uuid "ae842823-c28d-5956-a3bf-e70e9276c908" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397010} {:answer/id #uuid "42e3fb46-f61a-5833-95f6-27c46792783b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the fact that $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae842823-c28d-5956-a3bf-e70e9276c908" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397010} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac58334b-08c3-5e97-99f4-3dd187516d7b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d9118b1-b0ff-5db4-a05c-ec3ad938a6f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-337121" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L4}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Starting from $\\text{L4},$\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwe multiply both sides on the left by $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}$ to get\n\n$$\n({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L5}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides on the left by }({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L7}.$ Using line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c.\n$$\n\nFrom line $\\text{L6}$, we know that $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}).$ Substituting this expression for $c$ into the formula for $x(t)$ gives\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L7}.$ Thus, line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by $\\text{substituting }c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\text{ into }x(t)={e}^{At}c.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Since $At$ and $-A{t}_{0}$ commute, we can use the property \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into line $\\text{L7},$ we get line $\\text{L8}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}\\text{ when }X\\text{ and }Y\\text{ commute}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397012 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c0ef841-3242-5caa-a95a-63ce8b7efbf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397014} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1855a8-8668-5bad-a68f-159a347c16e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397015} {:answer/id #uuid "271ee91c-0505-593b-8b96-dcd47eee066b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397016} {:answer/id #uuid "ee36278b-f3db-5dd0-9d77-a7d3896daa39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397017} {:answer/id #uuid "416045ef-0621-54d9-bdb3-7210f39e7ecd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "271ee91c-0505-593b-8b96-dcd47eee066b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397016} :answer-field/id #uuid "23f571bd-1890-5d0b-ad01-ebacf978ce3f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397013} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6613fce0-00ea-54cc-b224-364324bfd38d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397020} {:answer/id #uuid "07ee30c0-36ff-5a79-9a4a-9d08de9626c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397021} {:answer/id #uuid "b953b3c5-d30e-55c3-84a5-1e9cfe455f31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397022} {:answer/id #uuid "a03f2f99-8a72-58f0-91c9-bed5f65cea3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397023} {:answer/id #uuid "40d5b092-c1ca-5934-8385-b0856ab2a919" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07ee30c0-36ff-5a79-9a4a-9d08de9626c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397021} :answer-field/id #uuid "e359f8f0-477c-59ef-8110-485977df974d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397019} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a8ade83-a027-534c-bd4f-84aa0200d2d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397026} {:answer/id #uuid "a5669714-9638-5173-9084-eb17dd7bd986" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397027} {:answer/id #uuid "ece141df-36de-5040-bd7f-fb517ce895fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{3x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397028} {:answer/id #uuid "9075b9b5-02ae-5817-9f6e-b66c5225cfc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397029} {:answer/id #uuid "25c082de-d2be-5ef1-b6ea-07729e875ea4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a8ade83-a027-534c-bd4f-84aa0200d2d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397026} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bedb308-447b-574c-bd8b-26248f559b30" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a01f9794-773d-5e12-a888-6dc684788a68" :question/math-academy-id "q-337376" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=5.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-3{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{3x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{3x})}^{′}-3(u{e}^{3x}) & =5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x}+3u{e}^{3x}-3u{e}^{3x} & =5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x}+\\cancel{3u{e}^{3x}}-\\cancel{3u{e}^{3x}} & =5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{3x} & =5 \\\\ {u}^{′} & =5{e}^{-3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & =5{e}^{-3x} \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{3x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{3x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}{e}^{-3x}\\cdot {e}^{3x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397031 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ac34a18-053d-5eab-8c2c-bd0f15658186" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c107f37e-7439-51cd-8125-7b533838b1a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397033} {:answer/id #uuid "7d799668-ca03-5716-985f-696822b47c93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\int {e}^{-x}(2x+5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397034} {:answer/id #uuid "8713ba55-0219-5ca2-aa75-e93b1a2aef1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}\\int {e}^{-x}(5-2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397035} {:answer/id #uuid "03d06967-2bd8-5ad1-ad41-704cc3be560a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}\\int {e}^{x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c107f37e-7439-51cd-8125-7b533838b1a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397033} :answer-field/id #uuid "008636f6-a3d9-555d-ad4c-a5efd04935ce" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397032} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a43a251-2319-5a92-9184-9e3033842d12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397038} {:answer/id #uuid "82de528b-a7d0-591d-bfd6-8981068dfdca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397039} {:answer/id #uuid "e73f10dd-6b3a-5dd0-bdff-640976047082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397040} {:answer/id #uuid "6459c483-0244-5e04-914d-7557e9e9be0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397041} {:answer/id #uuid "cb57fa42-6e17-53a6-b42d-1f4e39f65e1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397042}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6459c483-0244-5e04-914d-7557e9e9be0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(x){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397041} :answer-field/id #uuid "46425785-cb0c-5916-9859-40a15b476f37" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397037} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fc81de6-5f49-50eb-962c-7815ddf3c293" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-x}(5-2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397044} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5ccb87-cc4f-5977-af9d-3e72e6140cb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397045} {:answer/id #uuid "f883e0ee-9ac6-5e1d-8eda-78ecb99c56ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-x}(2x+5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397046} {:answer/id #uuid "cfba429b-73d7-56fd-a05b-13890a45950f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e5ccb87-cc4f-5977-af9d-3e72e6140cb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397045} :answer-field/id #uuid "80779cba-994a-51af-b9ca-eb4077594bf4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc82baf7-6e13-5137-9b62-5ced3f36541b" :question/math-academy-id "q-337395" :question/problem "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y=2x-5.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x)=$ {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the particular solution is ${y}_{p}(x)=$ {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}-{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable ${y}_{p},$ we set $A=u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=u(x){e}^{x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of ${y}_{p}$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate ${u}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{x})}^{′}-(u{e}^{x}) & =2x-5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{x}+u{e}^{x}-u{e}^{x} & =2x-5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{x}+\\cancel{u{e}^{x}}-\\cancel{u{e}^{x}} & =2x-5 \\\\ {u}^{′}{e}^{x} & =2x-5 \\\\ {u}^{′} & ={e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′} & ={e}^{-x}(2x-5) \\\\ \\int {u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${y}_{p}=u(x){e}^{x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\int {e}^{-x}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5fb547a-2518-5db9-b1b1-aab8d80328af" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Linear ODEs Using VOP When the Forcing Term is Part of the Complementary Solution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "544ef45e-9801-59af-90c5-d2e5923d0da8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397050} {:answer/id #uuid "7e87c929-0475-5c78-9a67-dac2d411868c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397051} {:answer/id #uuid "a0435832-f556-5180-9a87-eb33c09ea5ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397052} {:answer/id #uuid "19d94403-f572-5514-880b-e5648b1c55b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19d94403-f572-5514-880b-e5648b1c55b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{e}^