er/id #uuid "44414e5e-ea6c-5e29-8c97-658e69445da6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397439} {:answer/id #uuid "4e818916-b8da-55ed-9e45-159ab74b3b1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397440} {:answer/id #uuid "fef36346-1430-5b7e-8f8d-dbd4ef5452d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397441} {:answer/id #uuid "681611df-aafb-58e2-b2fd-60ed1c5a8c81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397442} {:answer/id #uuid "dca82b61-b202-5c4b-8b2a-4f67990862a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dca82b61-b202-5c4b-8b2a-4f67990862a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397443} :answer-field/id #uuid "d98a60af-8b0a-5156-82e3-3b9f66208118" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df849e8a-df1b-5b2f-bbc1-5b6e2ad9aeb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-340638" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{3}+5x$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{6}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{a}_{6}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{24}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-12\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & ={a}_{6}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ \\\\ {a}_{6} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩} \\\\ {a}_{6} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "304c015d-cbb6-5989-a102-d6f0f5f38604" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Expressions For Fourier Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5211e103-bbae-56b5-ab1d-86eeee675e89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397446} {:answer/id #uuid "549261c0-0dda-5beb-b854-9f2f8b637398" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397447} {:answer/id #uuid "eeadf2f7-53bd-5a77-9e67-80289734e565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397448} {:answer/id #uuid "a2c627de-a8e3-50ae-9a5e-cacf82786e25" :answer/type {:db/ident :a